//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
// Regression test for the fleet library (#283): the reference admission program
// `fleet/admit.vx`, unedited, must produce *different verdicts* on different
// SKUs. This is the paper's central claim, so it gets a test that fails loudly
// if a SKU declaration, the capacity math, or the const-folding of model-shape
// arithmetic regresses.
//
// The configuration in fleet/admit.vx is a 70B-class model at f16: ~120 GiB of
// weights alone, which does not fit an 80 GB card and does fit a 192 GB one.
//
// The RUN lines below reference `fleet/` relative to the repository root, which
// is the working directory the integration harness runs shell tests from.
//
// Rejected on H100 (80 GB), with the capacity numbers in the JSON record:
// RUN: not vxc --host default --machine fleet/h100-sxm.vx fleet/admit.vx --action emit-mlir -o /dev/null --diagnostics-json 2>/dev/null | FileCheck --check-prefix=REJECT %s
//
// Admitted on B200 (192 GB) -- same program text, only the machine file differs:
// RUN: vxc --host default --machine fleet/b200.vx fleet/admit.vx --action emit-mlir -o /dev/null --diagnostics-json 2>/dev/null | FileCheck --check-prefix=ADMIT %s
//
// The resident-set modelling rule (#286) holds: all three residents are placed
// in one function, so the working-set check sums them. An earlier draft split
// them across helper functions and a 100 GiB working set on an 80 GiB card
// compiled as *admitted* -- a false accept. This pins the tile count, which is
// what proves the sum actually happened.
// RUN: not vxc --host default --machine fleet/a100-40.vx fleet/admit.vx --action emit-mlir -o /dev/null --diagnostics-json 2>/dev/null | FileCheck --check-prefix=SUMMED %s
//
// This fixture's own body is inert; the RUN lines above are the test. It lives
// in `fail/` because that is the directory whose harness executes RUN lines.

fn main() -> i32 {
  return 0;
}

// REJECT: "verdict": "rejected"
// REJECT: "code": "E6009"
// REJECT-SAME: "space": "HBM"
// REJECT-SAME: "required_bytes": 128849018880
// REJECT-SAME: "available_bytes": 85899345920

// ADMIT: "verdict": "admitted"
// ADMIT: "error_count": 0

// The A100-40 record must show a working-set verdict over all three residents,
// not just the single oversized weight tensor.
// SUMMED: "verdict": "rejected"
// SUMMED: "tiles": 3
